  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="ipopodin-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">איפופודין</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾypwpwdyn</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">ipopodin</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="pos">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen">m.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="ipopodin-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>footstool</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>ὑποπόδιον</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>על דעתיהון דבית שמיי 
                     <app>
                        <lem>למלך</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#K V Ox1">משל למלך</rdg>
                     </app> שעשה לו כסא 
                     <app>
                        <lem>ואחר כך</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat2 K V">ומשעשאו עשה</rdg>
                     </app> 
                     <app>
                        <lem>האיפופודין</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#K V">איפיפורין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat2">אפיפודין</rdg>
                     </app> 
                     <app>
                        <lem>שלו</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat2">שלה</rdg>
                     </app></quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">1,15</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 13: 2</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>In the view of Bet Shammai this is parallel to the case of a king who first made his throne and then his footstool… (Freedman / Simon I 13)</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">LevR Be-ḥuqotai 36,1</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אפיפירון</term>); <bibl type="ancient">MShem 5,1 [28b]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אפופוריא</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 1 [2c: 19]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אפיפורין</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Yalq Jes 510 [406d: 51]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">איפופורין</term>); <bibl type="ancient">YalqM Jes 48,13 [168: 15]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">פורפירון</term>); <bibl type="ancient">YalqM Ps 102,20 [64b]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">פורפירון</term>, emend. <term xml:lang="jpa">אפופדין</term>]; <bibl type="ancient">yḤag 2,1 [786: 33]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אפיפודין</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Tanh (Mann) 15: 15</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">רגלים</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Midr (Mann) 37: 3</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אפיפרין</term>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Appears already in <bibl type="ancient">Targum Yer. to Ex 24,10</bibl> (cf. <bibl type="modern">Levy, Targ I 54b</bibl>). Cf. <bibl type="modern">AC I 226a-227a</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Levy I 138b</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Jastrow I 101a</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 39a</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Heijmanns (2013) 54</bibl>. The reading <term xml:lang="jpa">אפיפורין</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾpypwryn</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">apiporin</term> (attested in some versions of GenR and parallels, <bibl type="ancient">mKel 16,1</bibl> and 24,7, and in several other sources) shall be considered as a corruption (other etymologies for <bibl type="ancient">mKel 24,7</bibl> [cf. <bibl type="modern">Levy I 142b</bibl>] are not convincing, cf. Heijmanns). For <bibl type="ancient">GenR 17,6 (I 157: 8)</bibl> cf. <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">אפיפיון</ref>.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Sokoloff, DJPA</title>
                  <citedRange>26b</citedRange>
               </bibl>
               <bibl>
                  <title>Heijmanns (2013)</title>
                  <citedRange>54</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
